{
  "answer": "Requests enables HTTPS certificate verification by default: each Session starts with `verify = True`. A request can override this with `verify=False`, which disables certificate and hostname/expiry checks, or with `verify='/path/to/ca-bundle'`, which uses the specified CA bundle or directory. The `HTTPAdapter.cert_verify` method applies this setting to the urllib3 connection: truthy values set `CERT_REQUIRED`; a string is validated and configured as `ca_certs` or `ca_cert_dir`; false values set `CERT_NONE`. The separate `cert` option configures the client certificate, either as a file path or a `(cert, key)` pair.",
